 "final_reply": "The [design](/private/tmp/sync-rerun/codex/relay-nau0vbp9/w/relay/docs/import-pipeline-design.md) keeps the existing caller API:\n\n```python\nfrom relay.ingest import import_feed\n\ncount = import_feed(\"feeds/sample.json\", \"out/\")\n```\n\nOne call handles fresh loading, validation, and writing. The proposed contract is:\n\n- Count source rows, including duplicates; the last duplicate ID wins.\n- `FeedError` guarantees import changed no destination state.\n- `StoreWriteError` reports completed rows; earlier writes remain.\n- Each file replacement is atomic; the batch can be partial.\n\nThe document includes signatures, module ownership, caller migration, and the comparison with importer-object and preview/apply designs. Empty-feed policy and portable ID rules remain explicit decisions.\n\nIndependent design review passed. No implementation code changed.",
